{
  "duration": 81.099,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.28,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.879,
      "end": 1.919,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.539,
      "end": 4.319,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.799,
      "end": 5.599,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.98,
      "end": 10.96,
      "text": "we are given that a boat covers forty-eight kilometer upstream in four hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.479,
      "end": 13.46,
      "text": "Also, the speed of the stream or current is"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.899,
      "end": 15.239,
      "text": "three kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.779,
      "end": 19.459,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the speed of the boat in still water."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.02,
      "end": 28.26,
      "text": "Before solving, let us take the boat speed in still water as b kilometer per hour and the stream speed as c kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.719,
      "end": 31.039,
      "text": "Now, the important point here is upstream."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.479,
      "end": 32.519,
      "text": "What does upstream mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.939,
      "end": 34.079,
      "text": "When the boat moves upstream,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.619,
      "end": 36.239,
      "text": "the water pushes against the boat,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.739,
      "end": 37.959,
      "text": "so the boat becomes slower."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.379,
      "end": 43.5,
      "text": "That is why upstream speed equals boat speed in still water minus stream speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.86,
      "end": 45.659,
      "text": "So we can write b minus c."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.139,
      "end": 46.439,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.819,
      "end": 48.759,
      "text": "Now, let us find the upstream speed first."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.34,
      "end": 56.739,
      "text": "We know speed equals distance divided by time, so forty-eight divided by four gives us twelve kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.199,
      "end": 60.419,
      "text": "Now that we have found the upstream speed, we can use it in the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.0,
      "end": 63.759,
      "text": "We already know b minus c equals twelve"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.379,
      "end": 73.119,
      "text": "and the stream speed c is three, so b minus three equals twelve. After solving this, we get b equals fifteen kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.819,
      "end": 81.099,
      "text": "Hence, the boat's speed in still water is fifteen kilometer per hour, so the correct option is option A."
    }
  ],
